{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01Wny396pY3mzxFUW2cchvTr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. **Section 02 — Payment Security & PCI Compliance** is written and committed.\n\nThe file (`answers/02-payment-security-pci-compliance.md`, 599 lines) covers all 10 questions at senior/staff depth:\n\n**Core (7):**\n1. PCI DSS scope & SAQ A vs. A-EP vs. D tier comparison — why hosted fields collapse your compliance surface\n2. Stripe Elements postMessage mechanism — sequence diagram tracing iframe injection → user input → direct Stripe API submission → `pm_...` token returned\n3. Cross-origin iframe CSS isolation — why `appearance` config API serializes styles over postMessage, what's achievable vs. impossible\n4. CSP for Stripe checkout — full production header, directive-by-directive breakdown, the two most common misconfigs (`unsafe-inline`, missing `report-uri`)\n5. Tokenization lifecycle — Mermaid sequence diagram: PAN stays in Stripe's origin, only `pm_xxx` ever reaches your server\n6. Client secret storage risks — ranked `localStorage` (worst) → in-memory (correct), with XSS exfiltration example and bounded-blast-radius analysis\n7. Clickjacking defense — why `X-Frame-Options: DENY` doesn't conflict with Stripe iframes, `frame-ancestors` CSP, JS frame-busting as defense-in-depth\n\n**Deep (3):**\n8. Custom fonts in cross-origin iframes — what Stripe's `fonts` array actually does, CORS requirements, what's architecturally impossible, design compromise\n9. Pen tester's client secret finding — structured evaluation: what a stolen secret can/cannot do, five server-side controls required to make it safe\n10. Legacy SAQ D → Stripe SAQ A migration — phased rollout flowchart, cohort routing, Playwright PAN-detection test, WAF safety net, compliance validation checklist"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":307,"cache_read_input_tokens":46078,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":307,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18a147c2-8db9-4e3b-9844-4822e355c49a","uuid":"46ff7212-4d32-4b73-9c9b-d9008408d63c"}
